# X-Curse-Project-ID: fill in once a CurseForge project exists (see
# addon/DISTRIBUTION.md) -- some CurseForge tooling reads this to link
# an installed addon folder back to its project page. Left as a plain
# comment, not a live directive, until there's a real ID to put there.

# NOTE: Interface number above is DERIVED, not confirmed in-game: this
# machine's local install has a dedicated _anniversary_ client folder
# (separate from _classic_ and _classic_era_) reporting client version
# 2.5.6.69795 in .build.info under product "wow_anniversary" -- that's
# the live TBC Anniversary line. Applying Blizzard's usual
# major*10000 + minor*100 + patch Interface-number convention gives
# 20506. That convention usually holds but isn't guaranteed -- confirm
# with `/dump select(4, GetBuildInfo())` in-game and update this if it
# doesn't match. An out-of-date Interface number doesn't stop the addon
# from loading (with "Load out of date AddOns" enabled), it's only used
# for Blizzard's compatibility warning.

